arolina's 7th District leans Republican by about seven points, and incumbent David Rouzer is seeking another term with a commanding financial edge. He has raised roughly $2.5 million and holds $2.1 million on hand, while Democrat Kimberly Hardy has about $25,000 in cash after raising under $400,000. Neither side shows meaningful outside spending. Most independent raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, with several calling it Likely Republican.\n\nA late-August poll from a Democratic-leaning firm showed Rouzer ahead 45 to 39, and prediction markets give Hardy roughly a one-in-seven chance of winning. The national environment leans Democratic this year, which gives the challenger a plausible if narrow path, but the district's fundamentals, the money gap, and the ratings consensus make Rouzer the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0898, "margin": -8.11}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0938, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0915, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1198, "margin": -8.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0905, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0876, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0761, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0866, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1136, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1231, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.075, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1106, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1174, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.058, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0565, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -9.0}, {"d